 older: results from a national survey</article-title><source>J Am Geriatr Soc</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15450046</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ostbye</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Greenberg</surname><given-names>GN</given-names></name><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>DH</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><volume>1</volume><issue>4</issue><year>2003</year><fpage>209</fpage><lpage>217</lpage><article-title>Screening mammography and Pap tests among older American women 1996&#x02013;2000: results from the Health and Retirement Study (HRS) and Asset and Health Dynamics Among the Oldest Old (AHEAD)</article-title><source>Ann Fam Med</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15055410</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Levy-Storms</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Bastani</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Reuben</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name></person-group><volume>52</volume><issue>5</issue><year>2004</year><fpage>768</fpage><lpage>773</lpage><article-title>Predictors of varying levels of nonadherence to mammography screening in older women</article-title><source>J Am Geriatr Soc</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15086659</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Walter</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindquist</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Covinsky</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name></person-group><volume>140</volume><issue>9</issue><year>2004</year><fpage>681</fpage><lpage>688</lpage><article-